value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T11:45:31-07:00","id":517219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/515744-aeon-trinity-access-levels-above-omega?p=517211#post517211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alt post: you are not cleared for that information, citizen</div> </div> </div> </div>COMMUNIST DETECTED. ALL AVAILABLE TROUBLESHOOTERS ARE HEREBY SUMMONED TO FIND THE TROUBLE AND SHOOT IT.<br /> <br /> I never played Paranoia but an old friend of mine did. I think I remember him telling me that his troupe burned through clones the way most people eat.<br /> <br /> I just tried reading through the relevant sections of Trinity Storyteller's Guide to see if there were any official statements on what ALs above Omega were called. No dice.<br /> <br /> But I like the idea of color-coded Access Levels, so I came up with the following from lowest to highest: Omega-White, Omega-Gray and Omega-Black. (Hey, at least it's more imaginative than Omega-1, Omega-2 and Omega-3...but not by much, admittedly.) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T12:10:40-07:00","id":517228,"title":"","content":"Clearance level: Omega Black is the highest level of clearance and it sounds the coolest as is just and right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T16:48:19-07:00","id":517403,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd probably go for something like Omega Red, Omega Blue, and Omega Black.<br /> <br /> Or &quot;Omega Max&quot; since it's both the maximum AL and also Mercer may be the only one who has it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T20:32:38-07:00","id":517578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/515744-aeon-trinity-access-levels-above-omega?p=517228#post517228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearance level: Omega Black is the highest level of clearance and it sounds the coolest as is just and right.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/515744-aeon-trinity-access-levels-above-omega?p=517403#post517403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd probably go for something like Omega Red, Omega Blue, and Omega Black.<br /> <br /> Or &quot;Omega Max&quot; since it's both the maximum AL and also Mercer may be the only one who has it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have to keep in mind that there are only two more ranks above the Assistant Directors, who have Omega Clearance. Above the Assistant Directors are the Directors (Neptune's Neville Archer, Proteus' William Renton, and Triton's Maria Pappagallos), who would have an additional clearance level (call it either &quot;Omega+1&quot; or as I choose to call it &quot;Omega White&quot;).<br /> <br /> The only other known rank above the Directors is the Aeon Council, although it has been noted in the Trinity Storyteller's Handbook that the Aeon Trinity Directors are indeed members of the Council. The number of Council members is about 20 (see page 18 of the TSH), including the directors. Which brings up the question of whether the Council could classify something that not even the Directors could access? And if so, does that make the Directors subordinate to the Council? Would this be like the Politburo in having junior &quot;non-voting&quot; members and senior &quot;voting&quot; members? To extend the Politburo metaphor, would that mean that the Directors would sit on the Council as &quot;junior&quot; council members with only Omega-1/Omega-White AL and the &quot;senior&quot; Council members would have Omega-2/Omega-Black AL?<br /> <br /> And I don't think a higher &quot;Omega+3/Omega Max&quot; AL would exist. Aside from the fact that the only person(s) who could possibly outrank the Council would be Mercer (and Whitley), I think if the Council encountered something that was classified at an AL that <i>even the Council couldn't access</i>, it would be an immediate tip-off that Mercer was still around. Mercer's not that dumb, nor would I think that the Council would stand for having an AL that was beyond even them, especially since Mercer hasn't directly run the Trinity since 1950. Maybe the Council knows Mercer is still around in 2122, maybe not, but having an &quot;Omega+3&quot; AL that the Council couldn't access would be a dead giveaway that Mercer is still around or at least that <i>someone </i>in the Aeon Trinity outranked even them. If Mercer was trying to keep a low profile (and since 1950, he's always trying to keep a low profile) having an AL that only he could access would be a dead giveaway. Seriously, just imagine this conversation:<br /> <br /> Aeon Council Member: &quot;Computer, bring up File A01734. Authorization: Council Member [REDACTED], Access Level Omega-Black.<br /> <br /> Computer: <i>&quot;Unable to comply. Access Level Omega-Black is insufficient to access File A01734.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Aeon Council Member: &quot;How can that be? Access Level Omega-Black is the top AL in the Trinity!&quot;<br /> <br /> Computer: &quot;<i>Incorrect. Access Level Omega-Max is required to access File A01734.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Aeon Council Member: &quot;WTF is AL Omega-Max? <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ExplainExplainOhCrap\" target=\"_blank\">Who the hell could outrank an Aeon Council member-- <i>Oh shit, Mercer's back</i>.</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> *Sound of pants being soiled ensues*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":2710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","user":"Su-tehp","date":".  Soiling your pants while linking to TVTropes is especially not a good thing. 05-17-2015, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:33:31-07:00","id":527052,"title":"","content":"Maybe the better approach would be to avoid a name altogether. Things with names are more relatable and concrete, which seems to be at odds with how secretly the higher access levels conduct themselves. This could seem unimaginative, so hear me out:<br /> <br /> I don't think the time-travelling founder is common knowledge for the majority of membership. Even at Omega level, details on how/why Styles/Mercer or any other sufficiently inspired are still around are left blank - leading to much more suspicion of transhumanism than of time-travel. This is where Influence, Status: Aeon and other backgrounds start playing a greater role. An Omega cleared agent (probably a project head themself or working closely with one) with appropriately high other backgrounds will be exposed to these old hands eventually, but Clearance alone is built for facts and in some cases the facts are just too fuzzy to muddy the waters with. Although a footnote/attachment may be earned here and there for certain unsubstatiated reports (the Doyen jump to mind, rumors of aberrant activity, Psiads, etc..), such footnotes would rarely, if ever make it into the body text of a highly restricted document.<br /> The code for the 'super-Omega' operation (likely written in a barcode or some other machine writing) uses the identifying mark of Omega clearance - but modifies it with a few directions. Visually, only the most specialized computer engineer will be able to identify the marks without machine assistance, but never with less than a concentrated effort. For the most part, the maintenance engineers who might see the 'super-Omega' code show up in logs either don't have clearance to understand the arrangement of variables, or learn (truthfully) that Omega-level projects (like Rewrite) will sometimes be granted special investigatory powers pertaining to specific topics. A few top-flight, highly cleared security engineers of Aeon may understand what the variables actually mean, but these individuals are limited and will often be scraping the underbelly of inspiration at least.<br /> Here i might diverge from canon, using Tantalus as Mercer's own personal project (or creating a new name). After the identifier for Omega and Tantalus, a clearance hash of variables is often present and doesn't by itself mean anything. Tantalus, like many other projects are mutually exclusive and a Neptune or Rewrite Omega may not have access to the same information on the subject. Compartmentalization may be the only escape from transparency, as much as that would pain Mercer personally. So he has likely built a back entrance into the problem of clearance, if only for his own purposes - by the 2120s Mercer still has codes committed to his prodigious memory and can manually enter/recite twenty-plus digit numbers to access the Aeon records under a levfel of secrecy. I assume (non-canonically) this backdoor is Tantalus.<br /> <br /> An access level higher than Omega might fully translate out a something like: Omega Tantalus Priority, all topics, Rewrite edits visible, no logging. Effectively it's still &quot;Omega&quot; but now some extra parameters are added as needed for the current operation. Outside of operations, Backgrounds like Status and Influence are better measures of how close the character will get to a top-down perception of the whole mess. The council members likely aren't under the umbrella of Clearance, but their individual backgrounds and small number render such administration tools obsolete. The cheaters like Mercer and Styles aren't covered in the organizational stuff i remember from the Trinity PG, so they either exist outside of it or are simply agents with very unusual Clearance hashes allowing them all kinds of freedoms within the otherwise tightly restricted system. There may be access levels that even an older Mercer keeps from his younger self, the whole thing is probably a byzantine mess - i saw the pure Aeon allegiance as a way to cut through that - Agents like Hector Ramirez with strong backgrounds can ingratiate themselves to individual council members and by proxy influence the society as a whole.<br /> -shrug-<br /> <br /> TL;DR - There aren't any levels higher than Omega, just a selection of stackable Background masteries to purchase/obtain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T16:40:02-07:00","id":554985,"title":"","content":"I have long believed that the Access Level above Omega is Babel. Because of the &quot;Babel Dossier&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6463-proteus_est","name":"Proteus_Est","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:57:37-07:00","id":555366,"title":"","content":"Hello Proteus_Est, welcome to the board. Babel and Rewrite are two sides of the same coin, so it would make sense that they would have some advantages in figuring the whole thing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","cus